1. LOCKBIT
================================================================================
Ransomware Type: Ransomware-as-a-Service (RaaS)
Evolution: ABCD (2019) → LockBit 2.0/Red (2021) → LockBit 3.0/Black (2022) 
           → LockBit Green (2023) → LockBit 4.0 → macOS variant (2023)
Takedown: February 2024 (Operation Cronos) - infrastructure seized, 
          rebuilt, seized again. Still active as of 2026.

Attack Types:
  - Double extortion (encryption + data theft)
  - Triple extortion (encryption + theft + DDoS/threats to victims' customers)
  - Supply chain attacks
  - Exploitation of public-facing applications (VPNs, RDP, Exchange)
  - Data exfiltration via StealBit (custom tool built into LockBit 2.0+)
  - Ransomware deployment via GPO/SCCM for rapid lateral spread
  - PrintNightmare, ProxyShell, Log4Shell exploitation
  - VMware ESXi targeting for virtualized environments

C2 Infrastructure & Tools:
  - Cobalt Strike (primary C2 framework)
  - ThunderShell (HTTP-based RAT)
  - Ligolo (SOCKS5/TCP tunneling)
  - Plink (SSH tunneling on Windows)
  - FileZilla (FTP for C2/data exfiltration)
  - AnyDesk, Atera RMM, ScreenConnect, TeamViewer (remote access C2)
  - StealBit (automated data exfiltration tool)

